"use strict";(Array.isArray(self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs)?self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs:self.webpackChunkwoocommerce_multivendor_marketplace_docs=[]).push([[4386],{9350(e,t,r){e.exports=r.p+"assets/img/product-settings.67922411.webp"},97525(e,t,r){r.r(t),r.d(t,{comp:()=>i,data:()=>l});var s=r(20641),o=r(9350);const n={class:"hint-container tip"},a={},i=(0,r(66262).A)(a,[["render",function(e,t){const r=(0,s.g2)("RouteLink");return(0,s.uX)(),(0,s.CE)("div",null,[t[4]||(t[4]=(0,s.Fv)('<h1 id="selling-existing-products-select-sell" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#selling-existing-products-select-sell"><span>Selling Existing Products (Select &amp; Sell)</span></a></h1><p>In high-volume multi-vendor marketplaces, multiple merchants frequently offer identical brand-name goods, consumer electronics, books, or standard apparel. Creating separate product listings for every seller clutters the catalog, dilutes search engine ranking, and confuses shoppers with redundant duplicate pages.</p><p><strong>Selling Existing Products</strong> (powered by <strong>Select and Sell</strong>) solves this by enabling multiple approved vendors to attach their own pricing, stock, and offer notes to a single master product in the marketplace catalog. Customers enjoy a clean storefront with side-by-side merchant comparisons, while vendors easily list catalog items without re-entering descriptions or uploading media.</p><hr><h2 id="how-it-works" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#how-it-works"><span>How It Works</span></a></h2><div class="creation-modes-banner" style="margin:20px 0 24px 0;"><div class="creation-modes-banner__item"><h4><span>📦</span> Master Catalog Product</h4><p>A single canonical catalog listing created by the marketplace administrator or an approved merchant, establishing master titles, product images, categories, and attributes.</p></div><div class="creation-modes-banner__item"><h4><span>🏷️</span> Multi-Seller Offer Layer</h4><p>Multiple vendors attach competing offers to the same item—each specifying their own regular price, sale discount, stock count, and seller condition notes.</p></div></div><ol><li><strong>Master Catalog Item:</strong> A central product listing exists in the marketplace catalog with global images, categories, and descriptions.</li><li><strong>Vendor Offer Creation:</strong> Approved vendors search the marketplace catalog, select the product, and define their own regular price, sale price, inventory quantity, condition description, and draft/publish status.</li><li><strong>Storefront Merchandising:</strong> On the public product page, the marketplace displays the <strong>lowest active price</strong> by default, alongside the seller&#39;s custom note.</li><li><strong>Customer Comparison:</strong> Shoppers can inspect all competing sellers via an inline comparison table or an interactive popup modal, choosing their preferred merchant based on price, shipping speed, or seller rating.</li><li><strong>Automatic Order Routing:</strong> When an order is completed, revenue, tax, and commissions are automatically credited to the specific vendor whose offer was purchased.</li></ol><hr><h2 id="listing-an-existing-product-select-sell-flow" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#listing-an-existing-product-select-sell-flow"><span>Listing an Existing Product (Select &amp; Sell Flow)</span></a></h2><p>Vendors attach offers to catalog items through a dedicated 2-step onboarding screen:</p><p>Navigate to: <strong>Catalog &gt; List Your Product</strong> (<code>/seller/seller-list-product/</code>) → click <strong>Search Products</strong> (<code>/seller/seller-search-products/</code>).</p><p>Click the <strong>Search Products</strong> button to access the Select and Sell management console (<code>/seller/select-and-sell/</code>), then click <strong>Add Product</strong> (<code>/seller/add-selected-sell-product/</code>).</p><hr><h3 id="step-1-select-category-product-type" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#step-1-select-category-product-type"><span>Step 1: Select Category &amp; Product Type</span></a></h3><p>Select the taxonomy and architecture of the product you wish to sell:</p><ul><li><strong>Product categories:</strong> Choose the category under which the target product is indexed (e.g., <em>Clothing</em>, <em>Accessories</em>, <em>Decor</em>, <em>Music</em>, <em>Sports &amp; Outdoors</em>).</li><li><strong>Product Type:</strong> Choose between: <ul><li><strong>Simple product:</strong> Standard single physical or digital catalog item.</li><li><strong>Variable product:</strong> Products with variations (e.g., sizes or colors).</li></ul></li><li>Click <strong>Next Step</strong> to proceed.</li></ul><hr><h3 id="step-2-select-product-configure-offer-details" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#step-2-select-product-configure-offer-details"><span>Step 2: Select Product &amp; Configure Offer Details</span></a></h3><div class="language-text line-numbers-mode" data-highlighter="prismjs" data-ext="text"><pre><code><span class="line">Catalog &gt; Search Products &gt; Add Product</span>\n<span class="line">[Select Product*] ──&gt; Choose existing product from catalog</span>\n<span class="line">┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐</span>\n<span class="line">│ Default Author Product Info                                 │</span>\n<span class="line">│ [Thumbnail] Product Price: $16.00  |  Stock Status: Instock │</span>\n<span class="line">└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</span>\n<span class="line">Regular Price:   [ $14.50 ]</span>\n<span class="line">Sale Price:      [ $12.00 ]</span>\n<span class="line">Quantity:        [ 50     ]</span>\n<span class="line">Description:     [ Shown to customers below your price (0/300) ]</span>\n<span class="line">Status:          [ Draft / Publish ]</span>\n<span class="line"></span></code></pre><div class="line-numbers" aria-hidden="true" style="counter-reset:line-number 0;"><div class="line-number"></div><div class="line-number"></div><div class="line-number"></div><div class="line-number"></div><div class="line-number"></div><div class="line-number"></div><div class="line-number"></div><div class="line-number"></div><div class="line-number"></div><div class="line-number"></div><div class="line-number"></div></div></div><h4 id="field-specifications" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#field-specifications"><span>Field Specifications:</span></a></h4><table><thead><tr><th>Field Name</th><th>Type</th><th>Description &amp; Merchant Usage</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Select Product*</strong></td><td>Searchable Dropdown</td><td>Search and choose the specific marketplace product you want to sell (e.g., <em>Beanie with Logo</em>, <em>Long Sleeve Tee</em>, <em>Polo</em>).</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Default Author Product Info</strong></td><td>Preview Card</td><td>Displays the original author&#39;s baseline <strong>Product Price</strong> (e.g., <code>$16.00</code>) and real-time <strong>Stock Status</strong> (<em>Instock</em>).</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Regular Price</strong></td><td>Numeric ($)</td><td>Enter your custom retail selling price. Vendors can price competitively above or below the author&#39;s price.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Sale Price</strong></td><td>Numeric ($)</td><td>Optional discounted promotional price.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Quantity</strong></td><td>Integer</td><td>Enter the number of inventory units you currently hold in stock.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Description</strong></td><td>Text Area (0/300)</td><td>Enter specific condition or offer details (<em>&quot;Shown to customers below your price, for example the condition or what is included.&quot;</em>). Includes a live character counter.</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Status</strong></td><td>Selector</td><td>Choose <strong>Draft</strong> (saves privately in your vendor console to review later) or <strong>Publish</strong> (activates the offer immediately or submits it to the admin approval queue).</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Click <strong>Save</strong> to finalize your offer.</p><hr><h2 id="managing-your-offers-seller-select-and-sell" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#managing-your-offers-seller-select-and-sell"><span>Managing Your Offers (<code>/seller/select-and-sell/</code>)</span></a></h2><p>Vendors manage all active offers under <strong>Catalog &gt; Search Products</strong> (<code>/seller/select-and-sell/</code>):</p><ul><li><strong>Offer Data Table:</strong><ul><li><strong>Image:</strong> Master product thumbnail.</li><li><strong>Name:</strong> Product title. Hovering reveals quick actions: <strong>Edit</strong>, <strong>View</strong> public product page, and <strong>Delete</strong>.</li><li><strong>Price:</strong> Your active regular and sale price.</li><li><strong>Status:</strong> Badge displaying <em>Publish</em>, <em>Draft</em>, or <em>Waiting for Approval</em>.</li><li><strong>Stock:</strong> Current available units (e.g., <em>In stock (50)</em>).</li></ul></li><li><strong>Bulk Actions:</strong> Select multiple offers using checkboxes and choose from the <strong>Bulk Actions</strong> menu: <ul><li><strong>Delete:</strong> Removes selected offers from the store.</li><li><strong>Set as publish:</strong> Activates selected draft offers.</li><li><strong>Set as draft:</strong> Temporarily hides selected offers from storefront customers.</li></ul></li></ul><hr><h2 id="storefront-presentation" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#storefront-presentation"><span>Storefront Presentation</span></a></h2><p>On single product pages, customers can explore all participating merchants:</p><ul><li><strong>Primary Buy Box:</strong> Displays the lowest price among all active sellers, along with that vendor&#39;s custom description note.</li><li><strong>Other Sellers View:</strong><ul><li><strong>Popup Modal Mode:</strong> Clicking <em>&quot;More Sellers&quot;</em> opens an interactive modal window displaying merchant names, prices, feedback ratings, and individual <strong>Add to Cart</strong> buttons.</li><li><strong>List Table Mode:</strong> An inline comparison table renders directly beneath the primary product details on the page.</li></ul></li></ul><hr><h2 id="admin-configuration-governance" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#admin-configuration-governance"><span>Admin Configuration &amp; Governance</span></a></h2><p>Marketplace administrators configure global Select &amp; Sell settings, designate Global products, audit competing merchant offers, and moderate seller pricing from the WordPress dashboard:</p><p>Navigate to: <strong>Marketplace &gt; MP Select and Sell</strong></p>',34)),(0,s.Lk)("div",n,[t[3]||(t[3]=(0,s.Lk)("p",{class:"hint-container-title"},"Complete Administrator Guide",-1)),(0,s.Lk)("p",null,[t[1]||(t[1]=(0,s.eW)("For comprehensive instructions on managing Global vs Non-Global catalog items, search and filter controls, and administrative offer moderation, refer to the ")),(0,s.bF)(r,{to:"/documentation/admin-select-and-sell.html"},{default:(0,s.k6)(()=>t[0]||(t[0]=[(0,s.eW)("Admin MP Select and Sell Guide")])),_:1}),t[2]||(t[2]=(0,s.eW)("."))])]),t[5]||(t[5]=(0,s.Fv)('<p><a class="doc-image-link" href="./assets/product-settings.webp"><img src="'+o+'" alt="Select and Sell Admin Settings"></a></p><h3 id="key-administrator-settings" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#key-administrator-settings"><span>Key Administrator Settings:</span></a></h3><ul><li><strong>Enable MP Select and Sell:</strong> Master toggle to activate multi-seller offer functionality across the platform.</li><li><strong>Default Status As Global For All Products:</strong> When enabled, all newly published products in the marketplace are automatically marked as Global, making them immediately available for other vendors to sell.</li><li><strong>Seller Product Display Mode:</strong> Choose between <strong>Popup modal</strong> or <strong>List table</strong> for customer comparison on single product pages.</li><li><strong>Seller Email Notification:</strong> Automatically sends an order confirmation email to the vendor whenever a customer purchases their specific offer.</li><li><strong>Product Approval Queue:</strong> When product moderation is active, newly submitted Select &amp; Sell offers appear under <strong>Marketplace &gt; Product Approval</strong>, where administrators can inspect offer details, approve, or reject with a formal reason.</li></ul>',3))])}]]),l=JSON.parse('{"path":"/documentation/selling-existing-products.html","title":"Selling Existing Products (Select & Sell) Guide – WooCommerce Marketplace","lang":"en-US","frontmatter":{"title":"Selling Existing Products (Select & Sell) Guide – WooCommerce Marketplace","description":"Step-by-step guide for vendors and store administrators on using Select and Sell in WooCommerce Multi-Vendor Marketplace. Learn how multiple sellers can offer the same catalog product with custom pricing, inventory, and condition notes.","keywords":["woocommerce select and sell","selling existing products woocommerce","multi seller single product woocommerce","vendor catalogue offer woocommerce","marketplace buy box"]},"headers":[{"level":2,"title":"How It Works","slug":"how-it-works","link":"#how-it-works","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Listing an Existing Product (Select & Sell Flow)","slug":"listing-an-existing-product-select-sell-flow","link":"#listing-an-existing-product-select-sell-flow","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Step 1: Select Category & Product Type","slug":"step-1-select-category-product-type","link":"#step-1-select-category-product-type","children":[]},{"level":3,"title":"Step 2: Select Product & Configure Offer Details","slug":"step-2-select-product-configure-offer-details","link":"#step-2-select-product-configure-offer-details","children":[]}]},{"level":2,"title":"Managing Your Offers (/seller/select-and-sell/)","slug":"managing-your-offers-seller-select-and-sell","link":"#managing-your-offers-seller-select-and-sell","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Storefront Presentation","slug":"storefront-presentation","link":"#storefront-presentation","children":[]},{"level":2,"title":"Admin Configuration & Governance","slug":"admin-configuration-governance","link":"#admin-configuration-governance","children":[{"level":3,"title":"Key Administrator Settings:","slug":"key-administrator-settings","link":"#key-administrator-settings","children":[]}]}],"git":{},"filePathRelative":"documentation/selling-existing-products.md"}')}}]);